// wdoc section: Icons & Image Blocks.
page wdoc_icons { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Icons & Image Blocks" {}

  h2 "Icons" {}

  text {
    span "Full **Lucide** and **Bootstrap Icons** packs ship compiled into the binary. No runtime disk read; only used icons are emitted into the output sprite (`_wdoc/icons.svg`). Icons paint with `currentColor`, so colour follows the surrounding text or class." {}
  }
  text {
    span "Three ways to use an icon:" {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
// 1. Inline pattern in a span:
text { span "Status: :lucide.check: ready" {} }

// 2. Placeable icon block (a legal diagram child):
diagram {
  width = 80  height = 80
  icon {
    name = "lucide.compass"
    x = 10.0  y = 10.0  width = 60.0  height = 60.0
  }
}

// 3. Badge on a shape — any rect/circle/container/process/...
//    accepts icon / icon_size / icon_pos / icon_class.
process "Validate" {
  id = v  width = 120.0  height = 50.0
  icon = "lucide.shield-check"
  icon_pos = :top_right
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Iconsets" {}

  text {
    span "Declare an `iconset` to rename a pack or set default styling. Per-icon `icon_def` children override individual icons within the set." {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
iconset ui {
  pack  = "lucide"
  size  = "1.15em"
  color = "var(--wdoc-accent)"
  icon_def "heart" { color = "#bf616a" }
}

// Bare :name: now reads from the ui iconset:
text { span "We :heart: WCL." {} }
WCL
  }

  callout "Icons need serving" {
    class = ["note"]
    body  = "The icon sprite is referenced by <use href>, so icons only resolve when served or hosted — not via file:// directly. Same limitation as terminal fonts and tileset images."
  }

  h2 "Images" {}

  text {
    span "`image` embeds a static image at a fixed position inside a diagram. The source path is relative to the doc; the file is copied verbatim into `_wdoc/` at build time." {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
diagram {
  width = 400  height = 300
  image {
    source = "assets/logo.png"
    x = 10.0  y = 10.0  width = 200.0  height = 80.0
  }
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Tilemaps" {}

  text {
    span "A `tilemap` draws a 2D grid of indexed tiles cropped from a shared spritesheet declared with `tileset`. Authored numerically (`tiles: list<list<i64>>`) or symbolically via a glyph legend." {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
tileset platformer {
  source       = "assets/kenney-platformer.png"
  tile_width   = 16
  tile_height  = 16
}

diagram {
  width = 320  height = 240
  tilemap {
    set   = "platformer"
    scale = 2.0
    tiles = [
      [ -1, -1,  0,  0, -1, -1 ],
      [ -1,  3,  3,  3,  3, -1 ],
    ]
  }
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Dopesheets" {}

  text {
    span "`dopesheet` plays a range of frames from a spritesheet at a set `fps`. The bundled `dopesheet-player.js` advances the inner SVG viewBox frame-by-frame. Clicking the group toggles play/pause; set `loop = false` for once-through with a replay glyph." {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
diagram {
  width = 64  height = 64
  dopesheet {
    source       = "assets/pixel-coin.png"
    frame_width  = 16
    frame_height = 16
    fps          = 12
    scale        = 2.0
  }
}
WCL
  }

  callout "Hosted, not file://" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "Tilemaps and dopesheets reference their spritesheet by relative URL, so they only render correctly when served or hosted. wcl wdoc serve handles this for you locally."
  }

  text {
    span "Back to the [reference introduction](index)." {}
  }
}
